@startuml Use Case Diagram
title Leave Management System - Use Case Diagram
' Target use cases: PRD v1.3, BR-14/BR-14a, BR-19 and BR-20.

left to right direction

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam actorStyle awesome

actor Employee as Employee
actor SuperEmployee as SuperEmployee
actor Administrator as Administrator
actor "Configured Fallback\nApprover" as FallbackApprover <<assignment>>

SuperEmployee --|> Employee
Administrator --|> SuperEmployee
FallbackApprover --|> Employee

rectangle "Leave Management System" {
  package "Account" {
    usecase "Login" as UC_Login
    usecase "Change Own Password" as UC_ChangePassword
  }

  package "Leave Self-Service" {
    usecase "View Own Leave Balance" as UC_ViewOwnBalance
    usecase "Submit Leave Request" as UC_SubmitRequest
    usecase "View Own Leave Requests" as UC_ViewOwnRequests
    usecase "Cancel Own Leave Request" as UC_CancelRequest
  }

  package "Team Approval" {
    usecase "View Pending Requests\nfrom Direct Reports" as UC_ViewPending
    usecase "Approve or Reject\nDirect Report Request" as UC_DecideRequest
    usecase "Approve or Reject\nRequest Without Manager" as UC_NoManagerDecision
    usecase "Approve or Reject\nFinal-Stage Request" as UC_FinalDecision
    usecase "View Team Leave Calendar" as UC_ViewTeamCalendar
  }

  package "Administration" {
    usecase "View All Employees" as UC_ViewEmployees
    usecase "View Any Employee Balance" as UC_ViewAnyBalance
    usecase "Manage Employees" as UC_ManageEmployees
    usecase "Reset Employee Password" as UC_ResetPassword
    usecase "Adjust Employee Leave Balance" as UC_AdjustBalance
    usecase "Manage Holidays" as UC_ManageHolidays
    usecase "Manage Positions" as UC_ManagePositions
    usecase "Override Approval Decision" as UC_OverrideDecision
  }
}

Employee --> UC_Login
Employee --> UC_ChangePassword
Employee --> UC_ViewOwnBalance
Employee --> UC_SubmitRequest
Employee --> UC_ViewOwnRequests
Employee --> UC_CancelRequest

SuperEmployee --> UC_ViewPending
SuperEmployee --> UC_DecideRequest
SuperEmployee --> UC_ViewTeamCalendar

Administrator --> UC_ViewEmployees
Administrator --> UC_ViewAnyBalance
Administrator --> UC_ManageEmployees
Administrator --> UC_ResetPassword
Administrator --> UC_AdjustBalance
Administrator --> UC_ManageHolidays
Administrator --> UC_ManagePositions
Administrator --> UC_NoManagerDecision
Administrator --> UC_FinalDecision
Administrator --> UC_OverrideDecision

FallbackApprover --> UC_NoManagerDecision
FallbackApprover --> UC_FinalDecision

note right of UC_DecideRequest
  For requests with a manager,
  only the active direct manager may decide.
  This also applies when the requester
  or the manager is an Administrator.
  A requester may never decide
  their own request.
end note

note right of UC_NoManagerDecision
  Active Administrator other than the requester;
  if none exists, use the valid configured fallback.
  Approval completes in one stage,
  including requests longer than 5 working days.
end note

note right of UC_OverrideDecision
  Administrator only, while Pending
  or PendingFinalApproval.
  Reason: at least 10 characters.
  Decision Type: Override; outcome: Approve or Reject.
  Record outcome, stage and bypassed candidate context.
  A requester may never override
  their own request.
end note

note right of UC_FinalDecision
  Applies to requests requiring final approval.
  Active Administrator other than the requester;
  if none exists, use the valid configured fallback.
  The first-stage approver may also decide the final stage.
  A requester may never decide
  their own request.
end note

note bottom of FallbackApprover
  Assignment, not a new SystemRole.
  Must be active, configured and not the requester.
  May have the Employee role.
  Authority is limited to the eligible request and stage;
  it does not grant administrative or override permissions.
end note

note bottom of Administrator
  Permissions are cumulative through actor generalization.
  Access remains scoped to the resource and current hierarchy.
  Administrator status alone does not allow ordinary
  first-stage decisions for another manager's direct reports.
end note

@enduml
